    "prompt": "Historians point to several causes of the Mali Empire's power: its control of gold fields, its position on the trade routes between the Sahara and the Niger River, and the choices of its rulers, such as keeping order and supporting Islamic learning. Which cause mattered most? Write an argument with a clear claim and at least two pieces of evidence from the readings. Explain why your cause mattered more than at least one other cause, and when you use a source, say whose point of view it shows.",
